            <div type="apparatus">
                
            </div>
            
            <div type="translation" source="bib:Kuppusamy+al2010_01">
                <p n="1-8">...! On ... in the dark fortnight of the month of ... when the asterism was Uttirāṭam, in the
                    year ... <supplied reason="subaudible">of the reign</supplied> of ... emperor, śrī-Rājarājadevar, ... m-uṭaiyāḷ alias Maiyārkaṇṇi, the <foreign>tēvaraṭiyār</foreign>
                    of the temple of ... dhīśvaram-uṭaiyār ... of Uḻacciṉpulam in Muḻaiyūr-nāṭu in ...-nāṭu bought 100 <foreign>kuḻi</foreign>s
                    of nattam land from the temple after excluding the <foreign>devadāna</foreign> land of this deity, situated in the
                    <foreign>nattam</foreign> on the north side.</p>
                <p n="9-15">
                    As per the document of ... the amount was 300 <foreign>kāc</foreign>us the temple servants of
                    Āticaṇṭēśvara-tēvar of the temple of ... to the Tirunāvukkāraiyaṉ flower garden of ... this was the deed
                    in respect of the tax-free <supplied reason="subaudible">land</supplied> ... the eastern boundary for the land called ... to the north of ... the
                    western boundary was that it lay to ... of Vīra ...</p>
                <p n="15-21">
                    The land was given by pouring water for relief from illness to ... it was shown in the
                    registration office to ... rkaṇṇiyār ... was sold by him as tax-free ... when the question of paying the tax
                    came up ... given land ... sale price of gifted land ... the land sold as tax-free land for flower garden ...
                    Viḻiyūr-uṭaiyāṉ Araiyaṉ Uṭaiya-nampi alias ...</p>
            </div>
            
